I have a similar laptop, that literally runs nothing but nh-3.4.3.
It's running RedHat 6.2, but any copy of linux should work. Be wary of
distros like Mandrake though, as they build everything for a P6, not
the P5 arch that you have.

You could use Windows, and run the nice looking tiles version, but I
recommend that you stick with the console only linux one. Learning the
vi style keys is easy, it won't take you long to figure them out. Soon
it will be natural, and you'll wonder how you ever used those icky
keypads :)

